From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: route http state api and agent calls through connect proxy to reach isolated workers

With RAY_grpc_enable_http_proxy set, the head reaches other nodes' raylets and
agents over gRPC through the HTTP CONNECT proxy named by grpc_proxy,
https_proxy, or http_proxy. The dashboard's HTTP calls to the same agents do
not: the State API's runtime env query and the job head's calls to the job
agent open plain aiohttp sessions, so a worker that only the proxy can reach,
such as one on remote capacity behind a tunnel, cannot answer  or the job submissions and log reads routed to its agent.

The new NodeAgentConnector makes both sessions follow the same proxy choice as
gRPC, including no_grpc_proxy (or no_proxy when it is unset), tunnels each
proxied connection with CONNECT, and translates raw socket connection failures to
aiohttp ClientConnectorError. Without the gRPC proxy flag, nothing changes.

Upstream status: not yet reported to ray-project/ray.
